 ],
 "text": "9/30/26, 5:12 AM\ne Purchase contracts for small power producers, solar installations, and other forms of energy feeding.\n\ne Plant consumption contracts for generation and distribution installations of the utilities company.\n\ne Company consumption contracts, for example for the electricity consumption of offices at the utilities company\n\n1 Note\n\nService contracts (for example, for maintenance and repair) are not managed in this component; the Customer Service\n(CS) component is used instead. Service contracts are billed in the Sales and Distribution (SD) component.\n\nUse\n\nA contract is related to a division. It links one single contract account to one installation (see graphic for the master data (ISU-BF)\ncomponent). However, it is possible for several contracts to be grouped together in one contract account.\n\nA contract contains control data for Aontract Billing and Contract Accounts Receivable and Payable. These are:\n\ne General data (for example, contract account)\n\ne Move-in and move-out data\n\ne Schedule data (for example, start date and cancellation date)\n\ne Billing-relevant data\n\ne Account assignment data (for example, account determination ID)\ne Sales and distribution data\n\ne Deregulation data (for example service providers)\n\ne Data relevant to budget billing\n\nContract model: Where Does Data Originate\n",
